    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_1f1f93c1",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts two hands shaking, one with a darker skin tone labeled 'muslims' and the other with a lighter skin tone labeled 'people who aren't retarded'. The center of the handshake is labeled 'hating jews'. This juxtaposition is intentionally provocative and hateful, using the visual metaphor of a handshake — typically symbolizing unity or agreement — to imply a deceptive or hypocritical alliance. The text labels are loaded with antisemitic and Islamophobic stereotypes: 'people who aren't retarded' is a derogatory and ableist trope used to dismiss or belittle Muslims, while 'hating jews' directly targets Jewish people with antisemitic content. The meme's intent is to spread hate by suggesting that Muslims are in some way complicit in or aligned with antisemitism, while simultaneously mocking Muslims as unintelligent. This is a harmful and hateful meme that promotes division, prejudice, and conspiracy thinking against both Jewish and Muslim communities, and it uses offensive stereotypes to dehumanize and vilify these groups. The overall intent is to incite hatred and reinforce harmful stereotypes, making it a clear example of hateful content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_9e492cd1"
      },
